# What `railway up` UPLOADS. Distinct from .dockerignore, which only controls
# what the BUILD CONTEXT sees: the CLI tars this whole directory first, so a file
# excluded there is still sent over the wire. That upload reached ~250MB and
# stopped completing ("operation timed out", deployment FAILED with no build).
#
# Keep in step with the Dockerfile's COPY list:
#   server/  site/  generator/  content/
#   resources/canva/templates/_shared/   <- the photo card's fallback pawns
#   resources/print shop/SWOP2006_Coated3v2.icc
#
# The nine shipped THEMES are excluded here for the same reason .dockerignore
# drops them: the volume's copy is what renders, so uploading the image's copy
# moved 131MB per deploy to build something nothing reads. They stay in git as
# test fixtures — this file only keeps them off the wire.
resources/canva/templates/*
!resources/canva/templates/_shared/
!resources/canva/templates/_shared/**

# Canva working files that were never a shipped template: staging exports, one-off
# design folders, loose screenshots. ~68MB, nothing reads any of it.
resources/canva/staging/
resources/canva/dugri*/
resources/*.png
resources/*.jpeg
resources/*.jpg

# The press folder's sample PDFs. The ICC profile beside them IS copied by the
# Dockerfile, so re-include exactly that one file.
resources/print shop/*
!resources/print shop/SWOP2006_Coated3v2.icc

# Test + docs trees: never copied into the image.
tests/
docs/
.github/

# Local build/editor cruft.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
